WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.670
Our win rate fell from 29.7% to 27.1%.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.966
Did the team get worse at closing?

00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:12.976
Anna asks Canonic, and not

00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:15.046
just what changed, but why.

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:17.419
Canonic breaks the change apart into

00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:19.249
two parts, how much comes from the

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.219
mix of deals, and how much from the

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:23.409
rate at which the team closes them.

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:26.318
Small business, mid-market, enterprise.

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:27.478
Every segment closes

00:00:27.518 --> 00:00:29.188
more deals than before.

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:31.726
The team got better.

00:00:31.766 --> 00:00:33.696
The total fell because the campaign

00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:35.546
brought in more small deals.

00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:38.546
That mix effect costs 5.8 points.

00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:39.966
But within every segment,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.146
we closed better.

00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:43.476
The rate effect adds 3.3.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.924
Numbers tell you what changed.

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:49.744
Canonic tells you why.

00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:53.498
Canonic, let your agents

00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:55.668
query your data correctly.
